-- title:
--   Integrality of the rescaled logarithm of a commutative formal group
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, let $p$ be a prime whose image in $\mathcal O$ is a non-zero-divisor, and let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$: a $d$-tuple $F_i$ of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, with the coefficient of $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and of $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ in $F_i$ equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying the associativity identity; assume moreover that $F$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each $F_i$. Let $F_p$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in the same $2d$ variables with vanishing constant terms such that for every $i$ and every non-zero multi-index $m$ one has $\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_{p,i})\cdot p = p^{|m|}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$, where $|m|$ denotes the total degree; thus $F_p$ is the rescaled law $F(pA,pB)/p$. Let $\varphi$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms whose matrix of linear coefficients $\bigl(\mathrm{coeff}_{X_j}(\varphi_i)\bigr)_{i,j}$ is the identity, and which satisfies $\varphi_i \circ F_p = \varphi_i(A) + \varphi_i(B)$ for every $i$. Then for all $i,j$ and every multi-index $m$ on $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, the element $(m_j+1)\,\mathrm{coeff}_{m+e_j}(\varphi_i)$ lies in the ideal of $\mathcal O$ generated by $p^{|m|}$.
--
--   This is the integrality of the invariant differentials of a commutative formal group law, in the form of a $p$-divisibility estimate on the coefficients of the rescaled logarithm $\varphi(X) = f(pX)/p$, equivalently $m_j a_m \in \mathcal O$ for the coefficients $a_m$ of the logarithm $f$ itself. It is the integrality input used in the deformation-theoretic arguments concerning ghost components of Witt vectors and the Fontaine kernel attached to a formal group.
